        "title": "Two-thirds legislative vote to raise or create income taxes",
        "summary": "This amendment, proposed by the Iowa Legislature, would add a section to the Iowa Constitution requiring a two-thirds vote of the members elected to each chamber to pass a bill that raises the individual or corporate income tax rate (or another tax based on income or legal and special reserves), or that creates a new state tax on income. The rule would not apply to taxes local governments choose to impose. Any lawsuit claiming such a bill was not properly passed would have to be filed within one year of enactment.",
